    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday describes itself as an enterprise AI platform for HR, finance, and IT. Its website promotes Sana and agentic AI, saying that teams of specialized agents can perform key processes across HR, finance, and IT, and that its agents can find, build, act, and automate. Workday AI is listed as an ERP and business application AI product, with notes covering HR and finance AI, skills-based talent, predictive analytics, and sensitive HR data exposure.\n\nWorkday, Inc. is a public company headquartered in Pleasanton, California, founded in 2005, and trading as WDAY. SEC records list it under CIK 0001327811. Its most recent 10-K reports revenue of $9,552,000,000 for the fiscal year ended January 31, 2026. Court records list nine cases naming Workday, Inc. as a defendant in federal district courts in California, Georgia, Colorado, Maryland, and Virginia, including Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Inc. and Williams v. Workday, Inc. California accounts for 281 law exposure matters involving Workday.",
